-- ZacUI - the search index that ships with the settings window.
-- MADE BY tools/search_index (from the pages themselves, on the test
-- stand) - do not edit by hand. One piece of text per page; a page is
-- only turned into lines the first time someone searches, and the
-- text is let go then. Only this game version and class are kept once
-- the file has run. The search uses them only when `v` is exactly the
-- running version, so a build without a fresh one reads the pages as
-- before; the release check fails when this file is stale.
local ns = _G.ZacUI
if not ns then return end
local T = {
[=[return {c={"Auction tabs","Blizzard's window","Selling","Buy window","Price memory","What this does not do"},e={{"c","Auction tabs",1,1},{"t","Use ZacUI's auction tabs",1,1,"Adds three tabs below the auction window. Stands down automatically if Auctionator is loaded, since both would add competing tabs to the same frame."},{"r","Use ZacUI's auction tabs",1,1},{"r","Adds three tabs below the auction window.",1,1},{"c","Blizzard's window",1,2},{"t","Hide Blizzard's auction window",1,2,"ZacUI's window covers searching, selling and cancelling, so Blizzard's is usually just in the way. It stays one click away on the 'Blizzard window' button for its category tree and level filters, which ZacUI does not reimplement."},{"r","Hide Blizzard's auction window",1,2},{"d","Hide Blizzard's auction window",1,2,"ZacUI's window covers searching, selling and cancelling, so Blizzard's is usually just in the way."},{"t","Anchor Readycheck's consumables checker",1,2,"Readycheck opens its consumables checker when the auction house opens. This puts it beside ZacUI's window instead of wherever Blizzard's used to be. Drag it yourself once and ZacUI leaves it alone from then on."},{"r","Anchor Readycheck's consumables checker",1,2},{"r","Readycheck opens its consumables checker when the auction house opens.",1,2},{"c","Selling",1,3},{"t","Selling",1,3,"The Sell tab suggests the median remembered price minus this. One copper is enough to be the cheapest listing; larger undercuts only cost you money."},{"r","Undercut by",1,3},{"r","The Sell tab suggests the median remembered price minus this.",1,3},{"r","24 hours",1,3},{"r","Auction length",1,3},{"r","How long new auctions run. Longer costs a larger deposit.",1,3},{"c","Buy window",1,4},{"t","Layout",1,4,"The window that buys what you clicked. Card: the item, a bar of how far along it is, and the totals. List: each auction it will buy - seller, stack and price each - ticking off as you go."},{"r","Card",1,4},{"r","Layout",1,4},{"r","The window that buys what you clicked.",1,4},{"c","Price memory",2,5},{"t","Price memory",2,5,"There is no API that tells you what an item is worth. The only price data that exists is what the server sends while you browse, so ZacUI records the cheapest price it sees for each item and keeps the last ten observations. Prices you have never searched for are simply unknown, and old ones are shown with their age rather than presented as current."},{"r","There is no API that tells you what an item is worth.",2,5},{"r","0 items remembered",2,5},{"r","Forget prices after",2,5},{"r","Forget old prices",2,5},{"r","Forget everything",2,5},{"c","What this does not do",2,6},{"t","What this does not do",2,6,"No full-AH scanning. A complete scan hammers a rate-limited server, takes minutes, and is the single most common reason an auction addon gets an account disconnected. Every query ZacUI makes is queued behind the server's own throttle, and the price memory fills from searches you were going to run anyway."},{"r","No full-AH scanning.",2,6},{"b","General",1,0},{"b","Advanced",2,0}},t={{"general","General"},{"adv","Advanced"}}}]=],
[=[return {c={"Combined bag","Searching","Your other characters","Text on gear","Items you cannot use","Window style","Pinned row","Grid","Slots","Window","Text","Where the texts sit","The window","Reset"},e={{"c","Combined bag",1,1},{"t","Use ZacUI's combined bag",1,1,"Replaces Blizzard's one-window-per-bag layout. Turning it off needs a reload, because the bag keys stay pointed at ZacUI's window until the originals are restored at load."},{"r","Use ZacUI's combined bag",1,1},{"r","Replaces Blizzard's one-window-per-bag layout.",1,1},{"c","Searching",1,2},{"t","Searching",1,2,"Type in the bag's search box to fade everything that does not match. It matches the item name, its type and its subtype, so \"cloth\", \"potion\" and \"herb\" all work. A few single words are treated as filters instead:"},{"r","Type in the bag's search box to fade everything that does not match.",1,2},{"r","items tied to a quest you are on",1,2},{"r","quest",1,2},{"r","anything you can wear or wield",1,2},{"r","equip",1,2},{"r","grey items",1,2},{"r","junk",1,2},{"r","by quality",1,2},{"r","uncommon / rare / epic",1,2},{"c","Your other characters",1,3},{"r","Everyone's gold in the footer",1,3},{"d","Everyone's gold in the footer",1,3,"An Alts button beside the account total opens the list: each character in their class colour, their gold, and an x to forget one."},{"t","Remember every character's bags and bank",1,3,"Taken when you close the bag, open the bank and log out. The bag window gets a View dropdown to browse another character's items, read-only."},{"r","Remember every character's bags and bank",1,3},{"r","Taken when you close the bag, open the bank and log out.",1,3},{"t","Their counts on item tooltips",1,3,"\"Zacw: 5 in bags, 20 in the bank\" under any item another character holds."},{"r","Their counts on item tooltips",1,3},{"r","No character recorded yet.",1,3},{"t","Record now",1,3,"Takes this character's bag snapshot now (the bank too while it is open)."},{"t","Sample tooltip",1