[=[return {c={"The map layer","The seamless world map","What is under the map","What to show on the map","Readouts","Unexplored areas","You and your group","Heads up","Zoom and panning","Sharper map","Seeing through it","The window","Pins","Your arrow","Group dots","The game's own map","Zone name","Coordinates","Names under the group dots","When the map opens","Fading while you move","A change of map","The wheel's zoom","Battleground map","On the map","Seamless map","Look","Icons","Up close","When something looks wrong","Reset"},e={{"c","The map layer",1,1},{"t","Use ZacUI's map",1,1,"Replaces Leatrix Maps entirely. Run both and they will fight over the same hooks, so turn that one off."},{"r","Use ZacUI's map",1,1},{"r","Replaces Leatrix Maps entirely.",1,1},{"c","The seamless world map",1,2},{"t","The seamless world map",1,2,"Every zone stitched into one map; scroll out of a zone into its neighbours and the whole world, left-click to dive in, right-click to come back out, Ctrl-click to drop a pin. It brings its own window (drag its title bar, pull a corner), its own dungeon, raid, flight, boat and zeppelin icons and its own unexplored-area drawing, so those ZacUI settings stand down while it is on. Built on OpenMap (MIT)."},{"d","The seamless world map",1,2,"Every zone stitched into one map; scroll out of a zone into its neighbours and the whole world, left-click to dive in, right-click to come back out, Ctrl-click to drop a pin."},{"r","Use the seamless map",1,2},{"t","Seamless map settings",1,2,"Its settings are on this page's World map tab."},{"r","Seamless map settings",1,2},{"t","Choose the map style again",1,2,"The game's own map, the seamless map started closer to the game's, or the full seamless map. Going back to the game's own map takes a reload."},{"r","Choose the map style again",1,2},{"d","Choose the map style again",1,2,"The same choice is in the seamless map's own menu (Map style) and under /zuimap welcome."},{"c","What is under the map",1,3},{"t","Pieces on screen go behind the open map",1,3,"While the map window is open, a bar, an icon, a reminder or a text of ZacUI's that the map lies over is drawn behind it instead of on top, and comes back when the map closes. Windows opened over the map stay over it. A piece that holds buttons cannot change in a fight: it follows when the fight ends."},{"r","Pieces on screen go behind the open map",1,3},{"c","What to show on the map",1,4},{"t","What to show on the map",1,4,"Spirit healers, zone-crossing arrows and flight paths are on by default - they are most of the reason to run a map addon at all. If a category is on and you see nothing, /zui maps says whether this client actually has the art for it."},{"d","What to show on the map",1,4,"Spirit healers, zone-crossing arrows and flight paths are on by default - they are most of the reason to run a map addon at all."},{"r","Flight points, boats and zeppelins",1,4},{"d","Flight points, boats and zeppelins",1,4,"Yours. Boats and zeppelins are coloured markers rather than flight icons - the tooltip says where each one goes."},{"t","...and the other faction's",1,4,"Useful for knowing where not to land. Neutral points show either way."},{"r","...and the other faction's",1,4},{"r","Useful for knowing where not to land.",1,4},{"r","Dungeon and raid entrances",1,4},{"r","With the level range in the tooltip.",1,4},{"r","Dungeon and raid icons on continent maps too",1,4},{"d","Dungeon and raid icons on continent maps too",1,4,"Every zone's dungeon and raid entrances on the continent map; click one to open its zone."},{"t","Zone crossings",1,4,"Arrows at the zone borders. Left-click one to jump the map to that zone; right-click anywhere on the map to go up a level."},{"r","Spirit healers",1,4},{"r","Zone crossings",1,4},{"r","Arrows at the zone borders.",1,4},{"t","Hide Blizzard's town and city icons",1,4,"Only on the continent maps, where they collide with everything above. Recognised by the sprite they draw, which is the only handle Blizzard gives - so if a patch changes that art, this option quietly stops working rather than breaking anything."},{"r","Hide Blizzard's town and city icons",1,4},{"r","Only on the continent maps, where they collide with everything above.",1,4},{"c","Readouts",1,5},{"r","Coordinates",1,5},{"r","Your position and the cursor's, along the bottom of the map.",1,5},{"t","Zone level ranges",1,5,"Shown in the same strip. Hover a zone on a continent map to read its range without opening it."},{"r","Zone level ranges",1,5},{"r","Shown in the same strip.",1,5},{"r","Fishing skill required",1,5},{"r","A second number in brackets is the skill for the deep water.",1,5},{"c","Unexplored areas",1,6},{"r","Draw the parts you have not explored",1,6},{"t","Tint them",1,6,"Untinted, unexplored ground is indistinguishable from ground you have actually walked, which quietly turns the map into a lie. The colour and strength are on the Look tab."},{"r","Tint them",1,6},{"d","Tint them",1,6,"Untinted, unexplored ground is indistinguishable from ground you have actually walked, which quietly turns the map into a lie."},{"c","You and your group",1,7},{"r","Enlarge your own arrow",1,7},{"r","Blizzard's is 16 pixels, which on a full-screen map is a speck.",1,7},{"r","Show your group as class-coloured dots",1,7},{"d","Show your group as class-coloured dots",1,7,"ZacUI draws these itself and pushes Blizzard's own group blips out of the way - otherwise each teammate is drawn twice, in the same place, which reads as a smear rather than a marker."},{"r","Names under the dots",1,7},{"r","Each teammate's name in their class colour.",1,7},{"t","Leave off names that would overlap",1,7,"A group standing together shows one name instead of a pile of them. Zoom in and the rest appear as they spread apart."},{"r","Leave off names that would overlap",1,7},{"r","A group standing together shows one name instead of a pile of them.",1,7},{"c","Heads up",1,8},{"d","Heads up",1,8,"The seamless world map owns the zoom (one stitched world, wheel from the whole world to street level), so the zoom settings below and the sharper-map tiles stand down while the ZacUI World map part is loaded."},{"c","Zoom and panning",1,9},{"r","Zoom towards the cursor",1,9},{"d","Zoom towards the cursor",1,9,"Blizzard zooms about the centre, which makes finding a spot a cycle of zoom, pan, zoom, pan."},{"r","Scroll on into zones and back out",1,9},{"d","Scroll on into zones and back out",1,9,"One more wheel step past the top zoom level opens the zone under the cursor; one past the bottom level goes back up to the map above, zoomed onto where you were."},{"r","Allow zooming in further",1,9},{"r","How much further",1,9},{"t","Remember where you were",1,9,"Reopening the same map returns to the same place at the same zoom. A different map always opens fresh."},{"r","Remember where you were",1,9},{"r","Reopening the same map returns to the same place at the same zoom.",1,9},{"r","Keep the map centred on you",1,9},{"r","Hold shift to look somewhere else without it dragging you back.",1,9},{"r","Follow you between zones",1,9},{"d","Follow you between zones",1,9,"Only when the map is already showing the zone you were in - if you have gone to look at somewhere else, it leaves you there."},{"c","Sharper map",1,10},{"t","Draw zone maps from the game's minimap tiles",1,10,"Three times the detail of the painted map art, which an addon cannot replace. It is the minimap's picture of the ground - roads, water and buildings as they are - over the whole zone, explored or not."},{"r","Draw zone maps from the game's minimap tiles",1,10},{"d","Draw zone maps from the game's minimap tiles",1,10,"Three times the detail of the painted map art, which an addon cannot replace."},{"r","... with a solid sea under them, no painting through",1,10},{"t","... with a solid sea under them, no painting through",1,10,"Off, the painted map shows where there are no tiles and under see-through tiles. The sea colour is in the colour editor under Map."},{"d","... with a solid sea under them, no painting through",1,10,"Off, the painted map shows where there are no tiles and under see-through tiles."},{"r","... on continents too",1,10},{"d","... on continents too",1,10,"A whole continent is over a thousand tiles; untick this if opening the continent map stutters on your machine."},{"c","Seeing through it",2,11},{"r","Fade while you are moving",2,11},{"r","So the map can stay open while you ride somewhere.",2,11},{"r","Opacity while moving",2,11},{"r","Opacity while standing still",2,11},{"r","Stay solid under the cursor",2,11},{"d","Stay solid under the cursor",2,11,"Hovering the map while running is the one time you are definitely reading it."},{"r","The preview's Moving button shows the map as it is while you move.",2,11},{"c","The window",2,12},{"r","Header",2,12},{"r","Background",2,12},{"r","Line under the header",2,12},{"t","Line under the header",2,12,"Unchanged, each follows the theme on the Colours page. Advanced > Reset puts them back."},{"r","Coordinate strip",2,12},{"r","Unchanged, each follows the theme on the Colours page.",2,12},{"c","Pins",2,13},{"r","Icon size",2,13},{"d","Icon size",2,13,"Scales these icons together rather than flattening them to one number - a spirit healer is meant to read smaller than a dungeon portal."},{"r","Flight points, boats and zeppelins",2,13},{"r","Dungeons and raids",2,13},{"r","Spirit healers",2,13},{"r","Zone crossings",2,13},{"d","Zone crossings",2,13,"Each group on top of the icon size, for when one kind wants to stand out."},{"r","Outline each icon",2,13},{"d","Outline each icon",2,13,"Each one is drawn a second time behind itself, so it keeps its own shape and still stands out on busy terrain."},{"r","Outline colour",2,13},{"r","Outline size",2,13},{"c","Your arrow",2,14},{"r","Arrow size",2,14},{"r","Used when \"Enlarge your own arrow\" is on (General).",2,14},{"c","Group dots",2,15},{"r","Dot size",2,15},{"r","Small on purpose - a party standing together at 24 is one blob.",2,15},{"r","Dot colour",2,15},{"r","Class colour",2,15},{"t","Round",2,15,"Cut from a mask rather than drawn from art, because there is no filled-circle texture that can be relied on across builds. If your client has no mask support the dots stay square and /zui maps says so."},{"r","Round",2,15},{"r","The one colour",2,15},{"d","The one colour",2,15,"Cut from a mask rather than drawn from art, because there is no filled-circle texture that can be relied on across builds."},{"r","Outline",2,15},{"r","Keeps a dot readable over pale terrain and snow.",2,15},{"r","Outline colour",2,15},{"r","Outline width",2,15},{"r","Dot opacity",2,15},{"c","Unexplored areas",2,6},{"t","Colour",2,6,"Click to pick a colour. Right-click to reset it."},{"r","Tint colour",2,6},{"r","Also on the Colours page, and it travels with your profile.",2,6},{"r","Tint strength",2,6},{"c","Sharper map",2,10},{"r","Tile opacity",2,10},{"d","Tile opacity",2,10,"Below 100% the painted map shows through, which keeps its zone names and borders readable."},{"c","The game's own map",2,16},{"t","The game's fade while you move",2,16,"A separate fade from ZacUI's above: the game's own, which its options do not show. \"As the game has it\" leaves it alone; the other two hold it, and your own setting comes back when this is set back (or the Maps module is off)."},{"r","As the game has it",2,16},{"r","The game's fade while you move",2,16},{"d","The game's fade while you move",2,16,"A separate fade from ZacUI's above: the game's own, which its options do not show."},{"c","Zone name",3,17},{"r","Font",3,17},{"r","Font",3,17},{"t","Uses ZacUI's font (Fonts & Textures)",3,17,"Every text ZacUI draws is in the one font chosen on Appearance > Fonts & Textures. Size, outline and shadow are set here."},{"r","Size",3,17},{"r","Uses ZacUI's font (Fonts & Textures)",3,17},{"r","Outline",3,17},{"r","Shadow",3,17},{"r","Outline",3,17},{"r","Shadow X",3,17},{"r","Durotar",3,17},{"r","Shadow Y",3,17},{"r","Colour",3,17},{"c","Coordinates",3,18},{"r","Font",3,18},{"r","Font",3,18},{"t","Uses ZacUI's font (Fonts & Textures)",3,18,"Every text ZacUI draws is in the one font chosen on Appearance > Fonts & Textures. Size, outline and shadow are set here."},{"r","Size",3,18},{"r","Uses ZacUI's font (Fonts & Textures)",3,18},{"r","Outline",3,18},{"r","Shadow",3,18},{"r","Outline",3,18},{"r","Shadow X",3,18},{"r","Player 52.4, 38.1",3,18},{"r","Shadow Y",3,18},{"d","Shadow Y",3,18,"One font for the whole strip: your position, the zone's levels and the cursor's."},{"r","Zone level range",3,18},{"r","Your position",3,18},{"r","Cursor position",3,18},{"r","Decimal places",3,18},{"r","Say which is which",3,18},{"r","\"Player\" and \"Cursor\" in front of the numbers.",3,18},{"r","Your position",3,18},{"r","Format",3,18},{"r","Decimals",3,18},{"r","Letters",3,18},{"r","Default",3,18},{"r","Before it",3,18},{"r","After it",3,18},{"r","Template",3,18},{"r","Reads: Player 52.4, 38.1",3,18},{"r","Position",3,18},{"t","Reset",3,18,"Back to where it sits by default."},{"r","Reset",3,18},{"r","Point",3,18},{"r","Of the target",3,18},{"r","Anchor to",3,18},{"r","Where it sits now",3,18},{"r","X offset",3,18},{"r","Y offset",3,18},{"r","Text align",3,18},{"t","Text align",3,18,"Automatic, left, center or right. Automatic lines the text up with the point it hangs from."},{"r","Automatic",3,18},{"r","Cursor position",3,18},{"r","Position",3,18},{"t","Reset",3,18,"Back to where it sits by default."},{"r","Reset",3,18},{"r","Point",3,18},{"r","Of the target",3,18},{"r","Anchor to",3,18},{"r","Where it sits now",3,18},{"r","X offset",3,18},{"r","Y offset",3,18},{"r","Text align",3,18},{"t","Text align",3,18,"Automatic, left, center or right. Automatic lines the text up with the point it hangs from."},{"r","Automatic (right)",3,18},{"r","Zone level range",3,18},{"r","Position",3,18},{"t","Reset",3,18,"Back to where it sits by default."},{"r","Reset",3,18},{"r","Anchor to",3,18},{"r",