ou see.",5,53},{"c","Enemy name and marker",5,54},{"r","Name",5,54},{"t","Above the bar",5,54,"Inside: level on the left, then the name, health percent on the right. Above: the name floats over the bar."},{"r","Above the bar",5,54},{"r","Inside: level on the left, then the name, health percent on the right.",5,54},{"r","Name alignment (inside)",5,54},{"r","Centred",5,54},{"r","Raid marker",5,54},{"r","Above the bar",5,54},{"d","Above the bar",5,54,"Left end of the bar puts it before the level; the level and name step right while a mark is up."},{"r","Marker height above the bar",5,54},{"r","Above only.",5,54},{"r","Marker sideways",5,54},{"c","Friendly name and marker",5,55},{"r","Name (with a bar)",5,55},{"r","Above the bar",5,55},{"r","Name alignment (inside)",5,55},{"r","Left, after the level",5,55},{"r","Raid marker",5,55},{"r","On the bar, centred",5,55},{"r","Marker height above the bar",5,55},{"r","Marker sideways",5,55},{"c","Threat bar",5,27},{"r","Gap below the health bar",5,27},{"c","Simple aura row (older)",5,12},{"r","New lines go",5,12},{"r","Grows",5,12},{"r","Default (Right)",5,12},{"r","Default (Up)",5,12},{"r","Gap across",5,12},{"r","Per line (0 = one line)",5,12},{"r","Gap down",5,12},{"r","Reverse the order",5,12},{"d","Reverse the order",5,12,"Where its icons go when there are several. Its spot over the plate is under Fine placement."},{"c","Fine placement of the plate's parts",5,56},{"r","Enemy plates",5,56},{"r","Plates",5,56},{"r","Cast bar",5,56},{"r","Part",5,56},{"t","Reset",5,56,"Back to where it sits by default."},{"r","Position",5,56},{"r","Reset",5,56},{"r","Anchor to",5,56},{"r","Point",5,56},{"r","Of the target",5,56},{"r","Where it sits now",5,56},{"r","Y offset",5,56},{"r","X offset",5,56},{"r","Reset puts the part back where the settings above place it.",5,56},{"c","Priority mob count",5,46},{"t","Move it",5,46,"Shows the count with a sample line and unlocks it to drag."},{"r","Move it",5,46},{"c","Raid mod icons",5,57},{"r","Where",5,57},{"r","Under the bar, straight after the debuff row",5,57},{"r","Sideways",5,57},{"r","Up / down",5,57},{"r","Icon scale",5,57},{"c","Sunder / Expose - position",5,58},{"r","Measured from",5,58},{"r","Bar's right edge",5,58},{"r","Sideways",5,58},{"r","Up / down",5,58},{"c","Under the bar - position",5,59},{"r","Measured from",5,59},{"r","Under the bar, from its left corner",5,59},{"r","Row grows",5,59},{"r","Right",5,59},{"r","Sideways",5,59},{"r","Up / down",5,59},{"c","Reset",6,60},{"t","Reset nameplates",6,60,"Puts every nameplate setting back to ZacUI's defaults."},{"t","Reset debuff groups",6,60,"The debuff groups back to their standard layout."},{"r","Reset nameplates",6,60},{"r","Reset debuff groups",6,60},{"c","Custom debuffs",6,61},{"d","Custom debuffs",6,61,"Any debuff by spell id, or by name for a spell in your own spellbook; it joins the \"Under the bar\" row, muted until ticked there (General tab)."},{"r","spell id or name",6,61},{"r","Add",6,61},{"c","Soft target",7,62},{"t","Only active in raids and dungeons",7,62,"Ticked, the whole tab system (soft targeting, arrows, skulls, plate distance) arms only inside dungeons and raids and switches itself off in the open world. Untick to run it everywhere. Applies at the next loading screen, or at once when toggled here."},{"r","Only active in raids and dungeons",7,62},{"d","Only active in raids and dungeons",7,62,"Ticked, the whole tab system (soft targeting, arrows, skulls, plate distance) arms only inside dungeons and raids and switches itself off in the open world."},{"t","Mark the enemy the game is soft-targeting",7,62,"With nothing targeted: marks who you would pick up (the game's soft target). While targeting: the game will not soft-track a second mob, so the next-mob option below switches to ZacUI's own pick - your next mob by its ordering. Your target frame and normal targeting are never touched."},{"r","Mark the enemy the game is soft-targeting",7,62},{"d","Mark the enemy the game is soft-targeting",7,62,"With nothing targeted: marks who you would pick up (the game's soft target)."},{"t","Max nameplate distance while this is on",7,62,"Tab grabs mobs out to about 40 yards, but the picker can only rank mobs that have nameplates. This holds plates at the 41 yard cap (your old value comes back when unticked)."},{"r","Max nameplate distance while this is on",7,62},{"d","Max nameplate distance while this is on",7,62,"Tab grabs mobs out to about 40 yards, but the picker can only rank mobs that have nameplates."},{"r","Mark the target you would pick up when nothing is targeted",7,62},{"t","Mark the target you would pick up when nothing is targeted",7,62,"Off: soft targeting is never armed at all (the game's own behaviour while untargeted). The next-mob marker below works either way."},{"d","Mark the target you would pick up when nothing is targeted",7,62,"Off: soft targeting is never armed at all (the game's own behaviour while untargeted)."},{"t","Full-time mode - stays on while you fight",7,62,"On: never disarms, a soft pick lives alongside your hard target with the game's own circle, and hops to the next mob on kills. Off: soft targeting only while untargeted, with the arrows doing the marking."},{"r","Full-time mode - stays on while you fight",7,62},{"d","Full-time mode - stays on while you fight",7,62,"On: never disarms, a soft pick lives alongside your hard target with the game's own circle, and hops to the next mob on kills."},{"t","Full-time mode - stays on while you fight",7,62,"How far soft targeting will pick up a mob (active - soft targeting will not grab mobs beyond this). The Tab key still reaches about 40 yards whatever this says."},{"r","Soft target max range",7,62},{"d","Soft target max range",7,62,"How far soft targeting will pick up a mob (active - soft targeting will not grab mobs beyond this)."},{"t","Mark my next mob",7,62,"Ranked by distance from the centre of your screen - the rule Tab uses - wherever the game lets ZacUI read plate positions (it falls back to nearest-first with mobs on you at the top). Your current target and the two before it are skipped, like Tab. Click the marked plate (or tab) to take it."},{"r","Mark my next mob",7,62},{"d","Mark my next mob",7,62,"Ranked by distance from the centre of your screen - the rule Tab uses - wherever the game lets ZacUI read plate positions (it falls back to nearest-first with mobs on you at the top)."},{"d","Mark my next mob",7,62,"Screen-centre reading here: not sampled yet - needs a target and visible plates for a moment."},{"t","Also put Skull on the next mob",7,62,"Raid-marks the pick so it is obvious in the pile. Works solo or as party lead; does nothing when you cannot mark."},{"r","Also put Skull on the next mob",7,62},{"r","Raid-marks the pick so it is obvious in the pile.",7,62},{"c","Soft target arrows",7,51},{"r","Use ZacUI's coloured arrows",7,51},{"r","Off: the game's own plain icon.",7,51},{"r","Current arrow",7,51},{"r","Next arrow",7,51},{"t","Next arrow",7,51,"Current sits over the mob you are on (hard or soft target); next sits over the picker's next mob. Both have a 1 pixel black outline at any size. The pulse is on the Animation tab."},{"d","Next arrow",7,51,"Current sits over the mob you are on (hard or soft target); next sits over the picker's next mob."},{"r","Arrow size",7,51},{"d","Arrow size",7,51,"Arrows grow upward from the same spot, so making them bigger never shifts the plate or anything on it."},{"t","Keep arrows clear of the debuff icons",7,51,"Off by default - the arrows already draw on top of the debuff icons. On lifts them above the debuff rows instead."},{"r","Keep arrows clear of the debuff icons",7,51},{"r","Off by default - the arrows already draw on top of the debuff icons.",7,51},{"r","Arrow position - sideways",7,51},{"r","Arrow position - height above plate",7,51},{"t","Arrow position - height above plate",7,51,"Moves both arrows on every plate. 0 / 4 is the standard spot (centred, just above the plate)."},{"r","Moves both arrows on every plate.",7,51},{"c","Fighting with the marker up (macro mode)",7,63},{"t","Fighting with the marker up (macro mode)",7,63,"Instead of hard-targeting, aim your attacks at the soft target with a macro. With no hard target the marker never collapses, so it stays on screen the whole fight. Macro pattern:"},{"d","Fighting with the marker up (macro mode)",7,63,"Instead of hard-targeting, aim your attacks at the soft target with a macro."},{"r","/cast [@softenemy,harm,nodead][] Heroic Strike",7,63},{"t","Create RCSoft template macro",7,63,"Makes (or updates) a general macro called RCSoft with the pattern above; swap YourAbility for a real spell in Esc > Macros, then copy the pattern for each attack."},{"r","Create RCSoft template macro",7,63},{"d","Create RCSoft template macro",7,63,"The [] fallback means the same macro still works normally whenever you do have a target. /zui soft opens the soft target tools (dump, grassy, set, off)."},{"c","Crosshair",7,64},{"t","Show the crosshair",7,64,"Thin lines from the screen edges in to your target's nameplate, stopping at its edges and following it around. It draws over the world itself: turn it on and target something to see it."},{"r","Show the crosshair",7,64},{"d","Show the crosshair",7,64,"Thin lines from the screen edges in to your target's nameplate, stopping at its edges and following it around."},{"r","Cross sits on",7,64},{"r","My target's nameplate",7,64},{"r","Show",7,64},{"r","While I have an attackable target",7,64},{"r","Length",7,64},{"r","Full screen",7,64},{"c","Crosshair look",7,65},{"r","Line thickness",7,65},{"r","1 is a hairline.",7,65},{"r","Gap from the plate",7,65},{"r","Air between the plate's edge and where each line stops.",7,65},{"r","Soft shadow round the lines",7,65},{"d","Soft shadow round the lines",7,65,"A faint dark edge along each line and the centre dot, so even a hairline stands out on a bright or busy background."},{"r","Opacity",7,65},{"r","Colour",7,65},{"c","Reticle frame",7,66},{"t","Reticle frame",7,66,"A shape drawn around the plate itself, with the lines or instead of them. It follows the plate's size."},{"d","Reticle frame",7,66,"A shape drawn around the plate itself, with the lines or instead of them."},{"r","Shape",7,66},{"r","None",7,66},{"r","Padding from the plate",7,66},{"r","Frame thickness",7,66},{"r","Frame has its own colour",7,66},{"d","Frame has its own colour",7,66,"Off, the frame takes the lines' colour, range and warning colours included."},{"r","Centre dot",7,66},{"r","Frame colour",7,66},{"r","A dot in the middle of the plate, in the frame's colour.",7,66},{"r","Dot size",7,66},{"c","Colour by range and position",7,67},{"t","Colour by melee range",7,67,"Lines turn the first colour while an enemy you can attack is in melee range and the second when it is out. Friendly targets, and anything the game can't give a range for, use the colour above."},{"r","Colour by melee range",7,67},{"d","Colour by melee range",7,67,"Lines turn the first colour while an enemy you can attack is in melee range and the second when it is out."},{"r","Out of melee range",7,67},{"r","In melee range",7,67},{"t","Warn when I am in front of the target",7,67,"When it parries or blocks one of your attacks (which a mob can only do from the front), or swings at you in melee. The lines hold the colour below for 3 seconds and sit on top of the range colours. Leave it off when you tank."},{"r","Warn when I am in front of the target",7,67},{"d","Warn when I am in front of the target",7,67,"When it parries or blocks one of your attacks (which a mob can only do from the front), or swings at you in melee."},{"r","I am in front of it",7,67},{"c","Leave these alone",7,68},{"t","Leave these alone",7,68,"Units the cross treats differently, by name. 'No cross' hides it while that unit is your target - a boss where there is nothing to line up. 'No warning' keeps the cross but never changes its colour for that unit being on you. Click the tag on a row to switch."},{"r","Units the cross treats differently, by name.",7,68},{"r","Nothing yet.",7,68},{"t","Add my target",7,68,"Adds whatever you have targeted right now."},{"r","Add",7,68},{"r","unit name",7,68},{"r","Add my target",7,68},{"c","Plate scripts",8,69},{"t","Plate scripts",8,69,"MODS run hooks on every plate; SCRIPTS fire on a trigger (a cast, an aura, an npc). Code is a function: function(self, unit, envTable, modTable) ... end. self is the plate frame, envTable persists per plate per script, ZNP is the engine. Errors print once and never take the plates down."},{"d","Plate scripts",8,69,"MODS run hooks on every plate; SCRIPTS fire on a trigger (a cast, an aura, an npc)."},{"c","Mods (every plate)",8,70},{"r","New mod",8,70},{"c","Scripts (trigger-driven)",8,71},{"r","Edit",8,71},{"r","Example - red glow while casting",8,71},{"r","New script",8,71},{"c","Hook reference",8,72},{"t","Hook reference",8,72,"MOD hooks: Initialization (once, modTable only), Constructor (once per plate frame), Nameplate Added / Updated / Removed, Cast Start / Stop, Target Changed, Enter / Leave Combat. Updated ticks every 0.5s on every visible plate."},{"d","Hook reference",8,72,"MOD hooks: Initialization (once, modTable only), Constructor (once per plate frame), Nameplate Added / Updated / Removed, Cast Start / Stop, Target Changed, Enter / Leave Combat."},{"d","Hook reference",8,72,"SCRIPT hooks: OnShow when the trigger starts matching on a plate, OnUpdate every 0.5s while it matches, OnHide when it stops (also when the plate's unit despawns). Triggers are a comma list; numbers match spell/npc ids, anything else matches names."},{"d","Hook reference",8,72,"The disabled example script shows the working pattern: build widgets into envTable once, Show them in OnShow, Hide them in OnHide."},{"b","General",1,0},{"b","Look",2,0},{"b","Text",3,0},{"b","Animation",4,0},{"b","Position",5,0},{"b","Advanced",6,0},{"b","Soft target & crosshair",7,0},{"b","Scripts",8,0}},t={{"general","General"},{"look","Look"},{"text","Text"},{"anim","Animation"},{"pos","Position"},{"adv","Advanced"},{"soft","Soft target & crosshair"},{"scripts","Scripts"}}}]=],
