's ticked sections",0,4},{"r","Click the box, select all (Ctrl+A) and copy (Ctrl+C).",0,4},{"c","Import",0,5},{"r","Save as a new profile (optional)",0,5},{"t","Apply to this character",0,5,"A ZacUI profile string from another character, account or person. Checked for damage and read as pure data - nothing inside an import string is ever executed. Any other string ZacUI or Readycheck exports can be pasted here too: the line under the box says what it is, and the buttons offer to import it as that."},{"r","Apply to this character",0,5},{"r","Save as new profile",0,5},{"r","A ZacUI profile string from another character, account or person.",0,5}},t={}}]=],
[=[return {c={"Merchant","Mount macro","Weapon macros","World","Talking to NPCs by keyboard","Group","Small automations","General","Look","Text","Animation","Position","A timer that started without you","Advanced","Screen","Raid performance","Boss particles","Muted sounds","Buff remover","Macro cleaner","Unused macros","Bin","Auto roll","By quality","Known items","Your items","Junk items window","Low durability","Unspent talent points","Combat","Group deaths","Where they show","Instance reset and screenshots","Pet and tracking","Ready check","Loot feed","Boss loot","The card","Boss name","Items","Winners","Motion","Taking and handing in","Sounds and your party","Quest tracker","Character stats","Which stats","Rings round the cursor","Circle","GCD ring","Cast ring","Data blocks","Target distance"},e={{"c","Merchant",1,1},{"t","Sell junk automatically",1,1,"Greys sell when a vendor opens. Hold Shift while opening to skip."},{"r","Sell junk automatically",1,1},{"r","Greys sell when a vendor opens.",1,1},{"r","... print what it earned",1,1},{"r","item IDs, comma separated",1,1},{"d","item IDs, comma separated",1,1,"Exception list, both directions: a grey item listed here is KEPT, a white item listed here is SOLD."},{"t","Repair automatically",1,1,"From your own gold, silently skipped when you can't afford it. Shift skips."},{"r","Repair automatically",1,1},{"r","From your own gold, silently skipped when you can't afford it.",1,1},{"r","... print the cost",1,1},{"c","Mount macro",1,2},{"t","Keep one mount macro right on every character",1,2,"The macro named below is rewritten (out of combat) to use what this character has: inside the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj a Qiraji crystal from the bags, elsewhere the best mount item carried - epic before rare - or a paladin's or warlock's summon spell. Same key, every character."},{"r","Keep one mount macro right on every character",1,2},{"d","Keep one mount macro right on every character",1,2,"The macro named below is rewritten (out of combat) to use what this character has: inside the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj a Qiraji crystal from the bags, elsewhere the best mount item carried - epic before rare - or a paladin's or warlock's summon spell."},{"r","The macro's name, exactly as in the Macros window.",1,2},{"r","... make it (account-wide) when a character does not have it",1,2},{"t","Check now",1,2,"Prints what it picks on this character and writes the macro."},{"r","Check now",1,2},{"c","Weapon macros",1,3},{"t","Keep weapon swap macros on this character's weapons",1,3,"Every macro with /equipslot or /equip lines, on every character and class: a weapon the character does not have is swapped for its own in the same role (main hand, off hand, fast weapon, shield, off-hand item, two-hander, ranged), and a macro follows an upgrade of the weapon it used. Weapons you carry are never changed otherwise, so a set named on purpose stays. A macro with a #keep line is left alone."},{"r","Keep weapon swap macros on this character's weapons",1,3},{"d","Keep weapon swap macros on this character's weapons",1,3,"Every macro with /equipslot or /equip lines, on every character and class: a weapon the character does not have is swapped for its own in the same role (main hand, off hand, fast weapon, shield, off-hand item, two-hander, ranged), and a macro follows an upgrade of the weapon it used."},{"d","Keep weapon swap macros on this character's weapons",1,3,"Main and off hand: the pair you dual wield in boss fights, learned a few seconds into each pull - trash weapons worn on the way never count."},{"r","never in swap macros: Kingsfall",1,3},{"d","never in swap macros: Kingsfall",1,3,"Weapons never picked for a swap macro (comma between each) - trash weapons, say."},{"t","Check now",1,3,"Goes over this character's macros now."},{"r","Check now",1,3},{"c","World",1,4},{"t","Skip gossip pages",1,4,"Single-option gossip skips at stables, bankers, flight masters, trainers, vendors and battlemasters; elsewhere hold Alt. Shift suppresses."},{"r","Skip gossip pages",1,4},{"d","Skip gossip pages",1,4,"Single-option gossip skips at stables, bankers, flight masters, trainers, vendors and battlemasters; elsewhere hold Alt."},{"r","Faster auto-loot",1,4},{"d","Faster auto-loot",1,4,"Grabs every loot slot the moment the window opens, honoring master loot thresholds."},{"r","Dismount on error",1,4},{"r","Casting while mounted dismounts you instead of erroring.",1,4},{"r","... on no rage/mana/energy",1,4},{"r","... on 'can't do that while moving'",1,4},{"r","... when opening a flight map",1,4},{"c","Talking to NPCs by keyboard",1,5},{"t","Keys for gossip and quest windows",1,5,"1-9 pick a line: a gossip option, a quest on offer or in progress, a reward to choose. Enter accepts a quest, continues, completes it, or takes the first line of a list. Escape and typing are never touched; keys that mean nothing here go through to the game."},{"r","Keys for gossip and quest windows",1,5},{"d","Keys for gossip and quest windows",1,5,"1-9 pick a line: a gossip option, a quest on offer or in progress, a reward to choose."},{"r","... number the lines",1,5},{"r","... Space does what Enter does",1,5},{"r","... Space also presses a popup's first button",1,5},{"d","... Space also presses a popup's first button",1,5,"Release spirit, take the summon, enter the instance - popups that take no typing."},{"c","Group",1,6},{"r","Invite on whisper",1,6},{"d","Invite on whisper",1,6,"A whisper that is exactly the keyword invites the sender, when you can invite and are not queued for a battleground."},{"r","The keyword.",1,6},{"r","... friends only",1,6},{"r","Off, and anyone who whispers it gets invited.",1,6},{"r","... guild counts as friends",1,6},{"c","Small automations",1,7},{"t","Type DELETE for me",1,7,"The confirmation that asks you to type DELETE before destroying a good item is filled in; you still press the button."},{"r","Type DELETE for me",1,7},{"t","Open clams and crates on their own",1,7,"Clams, oozing bags, fishing trunks and the crates in the list below are opened when they land in your bags, out of combat, with a free slot, one at a time."},{"r","Open clams and crates on their own",1,7},{"r","more item ids, comma between",1,7},{"t","Skip cinematics",1,7,"In-game cinematics and movies end at once. Hold the key below while one starts to watch it."},{"r","Skip cinematics",1,7},{"r","Hold to watch",1,7},{"r","Shift",1,7},{"t","Accept a resurrection out of combat",1,7,"A resurrection offered while you are out of combat is taken at once, with a line in chat saying whose."},{"r","Accept a resurrection out of combat",1,7},{"t","Release at once in battlegrounds",1,7,"When you die in a battleground your spirit is released straight away (never in an arena, never with a Soulstone waiting)."},{"r","Release at once in battlegrounds",1,7},{"c","General",2,8},{"t","Show what goes off",2,8,"A small row of icons: every cast that went off adds its icon at the newest end, older ones move along. Under it a thin bar fills while the global cooldown runs. Nothing is on screen while the row is empty."},{"r","Show what goes off",2,8},{"d","Show what goes off",2,8,"A small row of icons: every cast that went off adds its icon at the newest end, older ones move along."},{"t","... show the presses too",2,8,"Every bar press adds an icon as well: dim while the game thinks about it, lit when the cast went off, red with a cross when it was refused (no rage, on cooldown). A refused press repeated is counted on its icon (x3) rather than filling the row."},{"r","... show the presses too",2,8},{"d","... show the presses too",2,8,"Every bar press adds an icon as well: dim while the game thinks about it, lit when the cast went off, red with a cross when it was refused (no rage, on cooldown)."},{"r","... the global cooldown bar",2,8},{"r","Icons kept",2,8},{"r","Gone after",2,8},{"r","Seconds after a press until its icon has gone.",2,8},{"c","Look",2,9},{"r","Icon size",2,9},{"r","Space between icons",2,9},{