l throws, /click ZacUISnowball RightButton clears - wherever you are, since only the mouse is held back by the lock (the game gives macros no way to know you are falling)."},{"r","Show a Snowball button that only throws in the air",4,8},{"d","Show a Snowball button that only throws in the air",4,8,"Click it as often as you like: on the ground it is locked and nothing happens; the moment you are in the air the same click throws a Snowball at yourself."},{"t","... explain in chat",4,8,"Chat lines on why a throw did not happen (locked on the ground, no Snowballs, the game's own error), and what a press of the mouse button did. Off by default."},{"r","... explain in chat",4,8},{"r","... only in raids",4,8},{"d","... only in raids",4,8,"Chat lines on why a throw did not happen (locked on the ground, no Snowballs, the game's own error), and what a press of the mouse button did."},{"r","... show the icon",4,8},{"d","... show the icon",4,8,"Off, and there is nothing on screen to click: only the mouse button (Advanced) throws."},{"r","Maexxna, Loatheb ...",4,8},{"t","Add a boss or trash mob...",4,8,"Only while targeting one of these (names, comma-separated; empty = always). Type names and press Enter, or pick bosses from the list (Readycheck's). Decided out of combat: target Maexxna before the pull and the button is up for the fight; the next change of target after the fight takes it down."},{"r","Add a boss or trash mob...",4,8},{"d","Add a boss or trash mob...",4,8,"Only while targeting one of these (names, comma-separated; empty = always)."},{"c","Look",4,9},{"r","Size",4,9},{"r","Changes wait for the end of a fight: the button is a secure one.",4,9},{"r","The cooldown sweep over the icon",4,9},{"r","The locked icon in grey",4,9},{"r","Locked tint",4,9},{"r","Back to the usual look",4,9},{"c","Text",4,10},{"r","How many you carry, in the corner",4,10},{"r","The count",4,10},{"r","Font",4,10},{"t","Uses ZacUI's font (Fonts & Textures)",4,10,"Every text ZacUI draws is in the one font chosen on Appearance > Fonts & Textures. Size, outline and shadow are set here."},{"r","Size",4,10},{"r","Uses ZacUI's font (Fonts & Textures)",4,10},{"r","Outline",4,10},{"r","Shadow",4,10},{"r","Outline",4,10},{"r","Shadow X",4,10},{"r","Shadow Y",4,10},{"r","Count colour",4,10},{"r","Count when you have none",4,10},{"r","Where the count sits",4,10},{"r","Position",4,10},{"t","Reset",4,10,"Back to where it sits by default."},{"r","Reset",4,10},{"r","Anchor to",4,10},{"r","Point",4,10},{"r","Of the target",4,10},{"r","Where it sits now",4,10},{"r","X offset",4,10},{"r","Y offset",4,10},{"r","Text align",4,10},{"t","Text align",4,10,"Automatic, left, center or right. Automatic lines the text up with the point it hangs from."},{"r","Automatic",4,10},{"c","Animation",4,11},{"r","When the lock opens and closes",4,11},{"r","Style",4,11},{"r","None",4,11},{"r","Duration",4,11},{"r","Delay",4,11},{"r","Easing",4,11},{"t","Repeat until hidden",4,11,"Pulse and Flash only: keep playing for as long as the frame is shown."},{"r","Repeat until hidden",4,11},{"r","Smooth",4,11},{"r","Comes from",4,11},{"r","Distance",4,11},{"r","Above",4,11},{"d","Above",4,11,"Only what you see: the lock steps aside the moment you leave the ground either way. None is how it has always been."},{"c","Position",4,12},{"r","Move it",4,12},{"c","Advanced",4,14},{"r","BUTTON4, ALT-BUTTON4, BUTTON5 ...",4,14},{"d","BUTTON4, ALT-BUTTON4, BUTTON5 ...",4,14,"A mouse button that throws only while you are in the air, wherever the cursor is over the world."},{"c","Screen",5,15},{"r","Remove screen glow",5,15},{"r","The ffxGlow cvar. Toggling off restores it.",5,15},{"t","Remove death and netherworld effects",5,15,"The ffxDeath and ffxNether cvars. Toggling off restores them."},{"r","Remove death and netherworld effects",5,15},{"r","The ffxDeath and ffxNether cvars.",5,15},{"t","Hide red error text",5,15,"\"You are too far away!\", \"Not enough rage\" and the like in the middle of the screen. Quest progress and other yellow lines still show."},{"r","Hide red error text",5,15},{"d","Hide red error text",5,15,"\"You are too far away!\", \"Not enough rage\" and the like in the middle of the screen."},{"c","Raid performance",5,16},{"t","Lower cosmetic graphics in raids",5,16,"Zoning into a raid drops shadows, SSAO, water, reflections, ground clutter and weather; zoning out restores exactly what you had. Ground markers are forced ON while active - spell effects, view distance and nameplates are never touched. Toggling this mid-raid applies immediately."},{"r","Lower cosmetic graphics in raids",5,16},{"d","Lower cosmetic graphics in raids",5,16,"Zoning into a raid drops shadows, SSAO, water, reflections, ground clutter and weather; zoning out restores exactly what you had."},{"r","Currently idle - it arms itself when you zone in.",5,16},{"c","Boss particles",5,17},{"t","Per-boss particle density",5,17,"Your particle WeakAura, native. In a raid the particle density sits at the raid level below (0 = off, for FPS on trash); when a ticked boss starts it jumps to the encounter level so particle mechanics stay visible, and drops back at the end - after the linger, for fights whose ground effects outlive the boss. Outside raids the world level below is set, or your own setting is put back exactly when that is off."},{"r","Per-boss particle density",5,17},{"r","Your particle WeakAura, native.",5,17},{"r","Currently idle - it arms itself when you zone into a raid.",5,17},{"r","Raid level (between bosses)",5,17},{"r","Encounter level (ticked bosses)",5,17},{"r","Set a level outside raids too",5,17},{"d","Set a level outside raids too",5,17,"Open world, dungeons and battlegrounds get the level below the moment you zone out of a raid, instead of whatever the raid happened to capture as your \"original\" - which is how particles got stuck on the lowest setting."},{"r","World level (open world, dungeons)",5,17},{"r","Naxxramas",5,17},{"t","Manage Naxxramas",5,17,"Ticked bosses get the encounter level. The box on the right is the linger: seconds particles stay up after the kill (Viscidus slime, Ouro residue). Blank or 0 means none."},{"r","Manage Naxxramas",5,17},{"r","Ticked bosses get the encounter level.",5,17},{"r","linger (s)",5,17},{"r","Anub'Rekhan",5,17},{"r","Grand Widow Faerlina",5,17},{"r","Maexxna",5,17},{"r","Noth the Plaguebringer",5,17},{"r","Heigan the Unclean",5,17},{"r","Loatheb",5,17},{"r","Instructor Razuvious",5,17},{"r","Gothik the Harvester",5,17},{"r","The Four Horsemen",5,17},{"r","Patchwerk",5,17},{"r","Grobbulus",5,17},{"r","Gluth",5,17},{"r","Thaddius",5,17},{"r","Sapphiron",5,17},{"r","Kel'Thuzad",5,17},{"t","Print encounter IDs to chat",5,17,"Every ENCOUNTER_START and END with its id, plus each density change. If a boss never triggers, this shows the id to fix in QoL_BossFX.lua."},{"r","Print encounter IDs to chat",5,17},{"r","Every ENCOUNTER_START and END with its id, plus each density change.",5,17},{"c","Muted sounds",5,18},{"r","Mute game sounds",5,18},{"r","City bell chimes",5,18},{"r","Spell fizzles",5,18},{"r","Interface clicks",5,18},{"t","Login screen music",5,18,"Muted at logout, so it takes effect from your next login screen."},{"r","Login screen music",5,18},{"r","Train emotes",5,18},{"r","Screech",5,18},{"r","Tiger yawns",5,18},{"r","Ready check and level-up",5,18},{"t","Piccolo of the Flaming Fire",5,18,"Also mutes warlock Seduction."},{"r","Piccolo of the Flaming Fire",5,18},{"r","Mute mount sounds",5,18},{"r","Mechanostriders",5,18},{"r","Mechanical steps",5,18},{"r","Horse hooves",5,18},{"c","Buff remover",6,19},{"t","Buff remover",6,19,"Needs Readycheck: the buff counting, hidden slots included, lives in its stats bar. Turn Readycheck on and reload."},{"d","Buff remover",6,19,"Needs Readycheck: the buff counting, hidden slots included, lives in its stats bar."},{"c","Macro cleaner",7,20},{"t","Macro cleaner",7,20,"Every macro in one list with a tick: delete many at once, see which ones nothing uses, and bring one back from the bin. Also /zui macros, and the Clean up button on the macro window."},{"d","Macro cleaner",7,20,"Every macro in one list with a tick: delete many at once, see which ones nothing uses, and bring one back from the bin."},{"r","Open the macro cleaner",7,20},{"t","Ask before deleting",7,20,"One question for the whole batch. Off, Delete deletes at once (everything still goes to the bin first)."},{"r","Ask before deleting",7,20},{"t","Clean up button on the macro window",7,20,"ZacUI's macro window has it in its footer; the game's own macro window gets it over its top right corner."},{"r","Clean up button on the macro window",7,20},{"d","Clean up button on the macro window",7,20,"By itself (all off until ticked; whatever it deletes goes to the bin like the rest)"},{"r","Delete on sight the macros on my always-delete list (0 names)",7,20},{"t","Delete on sight the macros on my always-delete list (0 names)",7,20,"For the macros another addon keeps making. The list is in the cleaner (the Always delete tab); a name gets there when you delete with \"...and delete them again whenever they come back\" ticked. Checked a few seconds after login and whenever the macro list changes, never in a fight."},{"r","Delete this character's own macros once they have gone unused",7,20},{"t","Delete this character's own macros once they have gone unused",7,20,"Unused: on none of this character's action bars and no key bound to it. Counted in days from the first login that saw it unused; checked a few seconds after each login."},{"t","...and account macros that no character uses",7,20,"Account macros are shared: one counts as unused only when no character seen so far has it on a bar or a key. A character that has not logged in since ZacUI started keeping track is not known - log into each one before ticking this."},{"r","...and account macros that no character uses",7,20},{"r","Unused for",7,20},{"r","Right now, unused for that long: 0 of this character's, 0 ac